Alternative: use the existing test suite (already covers it) plus run a real ps sample through a standalone replica for sanity. Actually — I can write a quick standalone Dart script that copies the exact regex + parse logic (verbatim from the file) and feed it REAL `ps -o lstart=` output from this host, plus check a mismatch case (recycled identity) and negative cases. That's a genuine negative/combination verification of the conformance claim.

Even better: verify with the REAL binary output piped in:

```dart
// /tmp/review/lstart_check.dart
